# CHECKOUT_ONLY — the shipped test suite's declared sdist scope.
#
# The sdist ships the full test suite, but the modules listed here
# audit the checkout itself: they import the checkout's tools/
# package, read docs/, examples/, .github/ or root files the sdist
# deliberately does not carry, or assume the development (editable)
# install's layout. In an sdist-only extraction they error at
# collection or fail at run time — measured, not guessed: the list
# is derived by executing the suite from an sdist extraction in the
# project's own test environment (see tools/sdist_scope.py, RR-12).
#
# Format: one module per line, "module | reason". The runner
# (tools/sdist_scope.py) verifies that the remaining declared scope
# — the base + posix test layers from tests/test_layers.json —
# collects with zero errors and runs green from the sdist alone.
# A module that gains a checkout dependency without joining this
# list fails that runner; a module listed here that no longer needs
# checkout content fails the manifest's honesty pins
# (tests/test_w5_sdist_scope.py). The hf layer is a separate
# environment scope ([hf] extra) declared in tests/test_layers.json;
# a module that is both heavy and checkout-bound appears in both
# declarations, so this list stays the complete census.
